{"id":"assistant-22f76cb8-1fde-58ad-bffe-8883eb45f5a7","sessionId":"49a4af54-fa21-5d2a-6347-9636d7d0322e","turnId":"turn-03f07ccab76bee470131e5a1329fcf26","inputEntryId":"user-turn-03f07ccab76bee470131e5a1329fcf26-1","createdAt":1794277072722,"updatedAt":1794277072722,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I understand the setup. The `kimi` lane runs under `sandbox-exec` with `agent.sb` profile which denies reading/writing to the real home directory. The Codex CLI writes its output to `-o \"$R/final.txt\"` where `$R` is in the user's home directory (under `runs/`), so this would be denied by the sandbox.\n\nBased on the colleague's note, the fix is to:\n1. Create a scratch folder in `/tmp` \n2. Point Codex's `-o` flag to that scratch folder\n3. After `sandbox-exec` returns, copy the files from scratch to the run folder\n\nLet me also check if there's a Codex CLI installed and understand its output flags:"}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
